    ($SATQ$9c0a0eca$SATQ$, $SATQ$7c5d80a9-e593-4cf8-b36b-bd89ed6226c7$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Area and volume$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">A triangle has a base length of <math alttext="10"><mn>10</mn>
</math> centimeters and a corresponding height of <math alttext="70"><mn>70</mn>
</math> centimeters. What is the area, in square centimeters, of the triangle?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"1de69c51-b821-4d54-8905-5313ad8b3340","content":"<p><math alttext=\"700\"><mn>700</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"56b4108d-ad52-48ff-b6b9-80751559d615","content":"<p><math alttext=\"350\"><mn>350</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"47380657-9fc9-49e0-aa41-08213bda9523","content":"<p><math alttext=\"175\"><mn>175</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"e0efe5b5-ee45-40e2-a4fa-85a359ee8efd","content":"<p><math alttext=\"80\"><mn>80</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["56b4108d-ad52-48ff-b6b9-80751559d615"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is correct. The area, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A"><mi>A</mi></math>, of a triangle is given by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A equals left parenthesis one half right parenthesis b h"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>b</mi><mi>h</mi></math>, where <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b"><mi>b</mi></math> is the length of a base of the triangle and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="h"><mi>h</mi></math> is the corresponding height of the triangle. It's given that a triangle has a base length of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="10"><mn>10</mn></math> centimeters and a corresponding height of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="70"><mn>70</mn></math> centimeters. Substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="10"><mn>10</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b"><mi>b</mi></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="70"><mn>70</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="h"><mi>h</mi></math> in the formula <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A equals left parenthesis one half right parenthesis b h"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>b</mi><mi>h</mi></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A equals left parenthesis one half right parenthesis left parenthesis 10 right parenthesis left parenthesis 70 right parenthesis"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mfenced><mn>10</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>70</mn></mfenced></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A equals 350"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>350</mn></math>. Therefore, the area, in square centimeters, of the triangle is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="350"><mn>350</mn></math>.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the product of the given base and height of the triangle, not its area.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is the sum of the given base and height of the triangle, not its area. </p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"9c0a0eca","external_id":"7c5d80a9-e593-4cf8-b36b-bd89ed6226c7","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"a8f28bca-3681-49bc-bf09-dfa29384fac2","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.A.","skill_desc":"Area and volume","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A triangle has a base length of <math alttext=\"10\"><mn>10</mn>\n</math> centimeters and a corresponding height of <math alttext=\"70\"><mn>70</mn>\n</math> centimeters. What is the area, in square centimeters, of the triangle?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"1de69c51-b821-4d54-8905-5313ad8b3340","content":"<p><math alttext=\"700\"><mn>700</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"56b4108d-ad52-48ff-b6b9-80751559d615","content":"<p><math alttext=\"350\"><mn>350</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"47380657-9fc9-49e0-aa41-08213bda9523","content":"<p><math alttext=\"175\"><mn>175</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"e0efe5b5-ee45-40e2-a4fa-85a359ee8efd","content":"<p><math alttext=\"80\"><mn>80</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["56b4108d-ad52-48ff-b6b9-80751559d615"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. The area, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi></math>, of a triangle is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals left parenthesis one half right parenthesis b h\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>b</mi><mi>h</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math> is the length of a base of the triangle and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math> is th