<div role="region" aria-label="Long description for diagram of 3 lines" class="sr-only"><ul><li>Clockwise from top left, the 3 lines are labeled script l, j, and k.</li>
<li>Line script l intersects both line j and line k.</li>
<li>At the intersection of line script l and line j, 2 angles are labeled clockwise from top left as follows:<br>
<ul>
<li>Top right: w°</li>
<li>Bottom left: x°</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>At the intersection of line script l and line k, 3 angles are labeled clockwise from top left as follows:<br>
<ul>
<li>Top right: 40°</li>
<li>Bottom right: z°</li>
<li>Bottom left: y°</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>A note indicates the figure is not drawn to scale.</li>
</ul></div></figure></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">In the figure shown, line <math alttext="script l"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></math> intersects lines <math alttext="j"><mi>j</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="k"><mi>k</mi>
</math>. Which additional piece of information is sufficient to prove that lines <math alttext="j"><mi>j</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="k"><mi>k</mi>
</math> are parallel?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"d5a774e6-e11f-4c64-ac30-4d9b92d23398","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"w equals 40\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>w</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>40</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"5390f2bf-f514-440f-9eff-f967cad663b6","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"x equals 140\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>140</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"55a393cb-287d-41ea-bd68-c079c6ac2795","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"y equals 40\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>40</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"1b0336f5-4c7a-416b-9a83-7f7073d9ff80","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"z equals 140\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>z</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>140</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["d5a774e6-e11f-4c64-ac30-4d9b92d23398"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is correct. In the figure shown, lines <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="j"><mi>j</mi></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="k"><mi>k</mi></math> are parallel if and only if a pair of corresponding angles are congruent. It's given that one angle has a measure of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="40 degree"><mn>40</mn><mo>°</mo></math> and that the corresponding angle has a measure of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="w degree"><mi>w</mi><mo>°</mo></math>. Therefore, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="w equals 40"><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn></math> is sufficient to prove that lines <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="j"><mi>j</mi></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="k"><mi>k</mi></math> are parallel.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. The angle measuring <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x degree"><mi>x</mi><mo>°</mo></math> and the angle measuring <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="40 degree"><mn>40</mn><mo>°</mo></math> are alternate interior angles. Thus, if lines <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="j"><mi>j</mi></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="k"><mi>k</mi></math> are parallel, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> is equal to <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="40"><mn>40</mn></math>, not <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="140"><mn>140</mn></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. The angle measuring <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y degree"><mi>y</mi><mo>°</mo></math> and the angle measuring <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="40 degree"><mn>40</mn><mo>°</mo></math> are vertical angles. Thus, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals 40"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn></math>, whether lines <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="j"><mi>j</mi></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="k"><mi>k</mi></math> are parallel or not.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. The angle measuring <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="z degree"><mi>z</mi><mo>°</mo></math> is supplementary to the angle measuring <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="40 degree"><mn>40</mn><mo>°</mo></math>. Thus, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="z equals 180 minus 40"><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>40</mn></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="z equals 140"><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>140</mn></math>, whether lines <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="j"><mi>j</mi></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="k"><mi>k</mi></math> are parallel or not.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"9d078710","external_id":"af20e9d4-dd92-4ae0-9ead-3798a3e06b80","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"4944038a-56ec-4562-bb60-904200e047dc","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.B.","skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg height=\"256.342457pt\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 234.357025 256.342457\" width=\"234.357025pt\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A diagram of 3 lines. Refer to long description.\">\n <defs>\n  <style type=\"text/css\">\n*{stroke-linecap:butt;stroke-linejoin:round;}\n  </style>\n </defs>\n <g id=\"figure_1\">\n  <g id=\"patch_1\">\n   <path d=\"M 0 256.342457 \nL 234.357025 256.342457 \nL 234.357025 0 \nL 0 0 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_1\">\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"></g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_2\"></g>\n   <g id=\"line2d_1\">\n    <