  <rect height=\"207.9\" width=\"209.25\" x=\"7.2\" y=\"13.43429\"></rect>\n  </clipPath>\n </defs>\n</svg>\n<div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for diagram of 3 lines\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul><li>Clockwise from top left, the 3 lines are labeled script l, j, and k.</li>\n<li>Line script l intersects both line j and line k.</li>\n<li>At the intersection of line script l and line j, 2 angles are labeled clockwise from top left as follows:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>Top right: w°</li>\n<li>Bottom left: x°</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>At the intersection of line script l and line k, 3 angles are labeled clockwise from top left as follows:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>Top right: 40°</li>\n<li>Bottom right: z°</li>\n<li>Bottom left: y°</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>A note indicates the figure is not drawn to scale.</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the figure shown, line <math alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> intersects lines <math alttext=\"j\"><mi>j</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math>. Which additional piece of information is sufficient to prove that lines <math alttext=\"j\"><mi>j</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi>\n</math> are parallel?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"d5a774e6-e11f-4c64-ac30-4d9b92d23398","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"w equals 40\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>w</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>40</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"5390f2bf-f514-440f-9eff-f967cad663b6","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"x equals 140\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>140</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"55a393cb-287d-41ea-bd68-c079c6ac2795","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"y equals 40\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>40</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"1b0336f5-4c7a-416b-9a83-7f7073d9ff80","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"z equals 140\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>z</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>140</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["d5a774e6-e11f-4c64-ac30-4d9b92d23398"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. In the figure shown, lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"j\"><mi>j</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi></math> are parallel if and only if a pair of corresponding angles are congruent. It's given that one angle has a measure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"40 degree\"><mn>40</mn><mo>°</mo></math> and that the corresponding angle has a measure of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"w degree\"><mi>w</mi><mo>°</mo></math>. Therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"w equals 40\"><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn></math> is sufficient to prove that lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"j\"><mi>j</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi></math> are parallel.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. The angle measuring <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x degree\"><mi>x</mi><mo>°</mo></math> and the angle measuring <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"40 degree\"><mn>40</mn><mo>°</mo></math> are alternate interior angles. Thus, if lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"j\"><mi>j</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi></math> are parallel, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> is equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"40\"><mn>40</mn></math>, not <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"140\"><mn>140</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. The angle measuring <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y degree\"><mi>y</mi><mo>°</mo></math> and the angle measuring <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"40 degree\"><mn>40</mn><mo>°</mo></math> are vertical angles. Thus, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y equals 40\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn></math>, whether lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"j\"><mi>j</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi></math> are parallel or not.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. The angle measuring <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"z degree\"><mi>z</mi><mo>°</mo></math> is supplementary to the angle measuring <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"40 degree\"><mn>40</mn><mo>°</mo></math>. Thus, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"z equals 180 minus 40\"><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>40</mn></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"z equals 140\"><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>140</mn></math>, whether lines <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"j\"><mi>j</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi></math> are parallel or not.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1755117017722,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"9d078710","skill_cd":"S.B.","score_band_range_cd":3,"skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","createDate":1755117017722,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"","external_id":"af20e9d4-dd92-4ae0-9ead-3798a3e06b80","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"4944038a-56ec-4562-bb60-904200e047dc","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg height=\"256.342457pt