s in the form <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus h right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus k right parenthesis squared equals r squared\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, where <math alttext=\"h equals 4\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>, <math alttext=\"k equals 9\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math>, and <math alttext=\"r equals 4\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>, and represents a circle in the <em>xy</em>-plane with center <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 4 comma 9 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and radius of length <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi>\n</math> in the equation <math alttext=\"r equals StartAbsoluteValue h EndAbsoluteValue\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mi>h</mi></mfenced></math> yields <math alttext=\"4 equals StartAbsoluteValue 4 EndAbsoluteValue\"><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mn>4</mn></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext=\"4 equals 4\"><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>, which is true. Therefore, the equation in choice C represents a circle in the <em>xy</em>-plane that intersects the <em>y</em>-axis at exactly one point.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the equation of a circle that does not intersect the <em>y</em>-axis at any point.</p>\n<p>Choice B is incorrect. This is an equation of a circle that intersects the <em>x</em>-axis, not the <em>y</em>-axis, at exactly one point.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is the equation of a circle with the center located on the <em>y</em>-axis and thus intersects the <em>y</em>-axis at exactly two points, not exactly one point.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":"manifold","position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959840,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"9d159400","skill_cd":"S.D.","score_band_range_cd":7,"skill_desc":"Circles","createDate":1691007959840,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":null,"external_id":"78306704-22d8-4501-a060-e7b7995c3ceb","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"a904ec9c-4c1f-447f-91ee-8fef470bedbb","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"keys":["71902793-1d5c-4354-9d38-2bbc06bcf133"],"rationale":"<p>Choice C is correct. The graph of the equation&nbsp;<math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus h right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus k right parenthesis squared equals r squared\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> in the <em>xy</em>-plane is a circle with center&nbsp;<math alttext=\"left parenthesis h comma k right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and a radius of length <math alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi>\n</math>. The radius of a circle is the distance from the center of the circle to any point on the circle. If a circle in the <em>xy</em>-plane intersects the <em>y</em>-axis at exactly one point, then the perpendicular distance from the center of the circle to this point on the <em>y</em>-axis must be equal to the length of the circle's radius. It follows that the <em>x</em>-coordinate of the circle's center must be equivalent to the length of the circle's radius. In other words, if the graph of <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus h right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus k right parenthesis squared equals r squared\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is a circle that intersects the <em>y</em>-axis at exactly one point, then <math alttext=\"r equals StartAbsoluteValue h EndAbsoluteValue\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mi>h</mi></mfenced></math> must be true. The equation in choice C is <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 4 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 9 right parenthesis squared equals 16\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 4 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 9 right parenthesis squared equals 4 squared\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. This equation is in the form <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus h right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus k right parenthesis squared equals r squared\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, where <math alttext=\"h equals 4\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>, <math alttext=\"k equals 9\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math>, and <math alttext=\"r equals 4\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>, and represents a circle in the <em>xy</em>-plane with center <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 4 comma 9 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and radius of length <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi>\n</math> in the equation <math alttext=\"r equals StartAbsoluteValue h EndAbsoluteValue\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mi>h</mi></mfenced></math> yields <math alttext=\"4 equals StartAbsoluteValue 4 EndAbsoluteValue\"><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mn>4</mn></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext=\"4 equals 4\"><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>, which is true. Therefore, the equation in choice C represents a circle in the <em>xy</em>-plane that intersects the <em>y</em>-axis at exactly one point.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the equation of a circle that does not intersect the <em>y</em>-axis at any point.</p>\n<p>Choice B is incorrect. This is an equation of a circle that intersects the <em>x</em>-axis, not the <em>y</em>-axis, at exactly one point.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is the equation of a circle with the center located on the <em>y</em>-axis and thus intersects the <em>y</em>-axis at exactly two points, not exactly one point.</p>","origin":"manifold","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Which of the following equations represents a circle in the <em>xy</em>-plane that intersects the <em>y</em>-axis at exactly one point?</p>","externalid":"78306704-22d8-4501-a060-e7b7995c3ceb","templateid":"7edeffa7-6afc-4c01-a321-c025db5892c6","vaultid":"94272fab-d8eb-4bbb-8d43-d434e0d28143","type":"mcq","answerOptions":[{"id":"806b400d-a2bc-4eea-a14c-5494e0cb61a5","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 8 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 8 right parenthesis squared equals 16\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>8</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>8</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>16</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"1c23b20a-efbe-45a1-81b7-76cd72c417eb","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 8 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 4 right parenthesis squared equals 16\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>8</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>16</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"71902793-1d5c-4354-9d38-2bbc06bcf133","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 4 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 9 right parenthesis squared equals 16\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>9</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>16</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"b2e76211-cf69-4443-9d95-1940a7c4b097","content":"<p><math alttext=\"x squared plus left parenthesis y minus 9 right parenthesis squared equals 16\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>9</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>16</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}],"correct_answer":["C"]},"createDate":1691007959840,"updateDate":1691007959840}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959840, 1691007959840),
    ($SATQ$9d2e7037$SATQ$, $SATQ$5a173e5b-ac90-4f05-806e-fe38d80fcfd9$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Area and volume$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">A rectangle has a length of <math alttext="56"><mn>56</mn>
</math> inches and a width of <math alttext="28"><mn>28</mn>
</math> inches. What is the area, in square inches, of the rectangle?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"b303c554-6e6e-4eb9-9b98-bba530461ca2","content":"<p><math alttext=\"28\"><mn>28</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"d502ddec-d756-4e33-9a84-926602076c43","content":"<p><math alttext=\"84\"><mn>84</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"71a275dc-04d8-41c0-971c-d2b494601e00","content":"<p><math alttext=\"168\"><mn>168</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"83e1846a-7e85-4815-a694-3ed9dad450d8","content":"<p><math alttext=\"1,568\"><mn>1,568</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["83e1846a-7e85-4815-a694-3ed9dad450d8"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. The area, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A"><mi>A</mi></math>, of a rectangle can be found using the formula <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A equals script l w"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mi>w</mi></math>, where <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="script l"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></math>&nbsp;represents the length and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="w"><mi>w</mi></math> represents the width of the rectangle. It&rsquo;s given that a rectangle has a length of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="56"><mn>56</mn></math> inches and a width of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="28"><mn>28</mn></math> inches. Substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="56"><mn>56</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="script l"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="28"><mn>28</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="w"><mi>w</mi></math> in the formula <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A equals script l w"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mi>w</mi></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A equals left parenthesis 56 right parenthesis left parenthesis 28 right parenthesis"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper A equals 1,568"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1,568</mn></math>. Therefore, the area, in square inches, of the rectangle is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1,568"><mn>1,568</mn></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This is the width, in inches, not the area, in square inches, of the rectangle.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"9d2e7037","external_id":"5a173e5b-ac90-4f05-806e-fe38d80fcfd9","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"fb1e3adb-3c22-4961-89ee-0fe2391aae40","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.A.","skill_desc":"Area and volume","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A rectangle has a length of <math alttext=\"56\"><mn>56</mn>\n</math> inches and a width of <math alttext=\"28\"><mn>28</mn>\n</math> inches. What is the area, in square inches, of the rectangle?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"b303c554-6e6e-4eb9-9b98-bba530461ca2","content":"<p><math alttext=\"28\"><mn>28</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"d502ddec-d756-4e33-9a84-926602076c43","content":"<p><math alttext=\"84\"><mn>84</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"71a275dc-04d8-41c0-971c-d2b494601e00","content":"<p><math alttext=\"168\"><mn>168</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"83e1846a-7e85-4815-a694-3ed9dad450d8","content":"<p><math alttext=\"1,568\"><mn>1,568</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["83e1846a-7e85-4815-a694-3ed9dad450d8"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. The area, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi></math>, of a rectangle can be found using the formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals script l w\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mi>w</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math>&nbsp;represents the length and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi></math> represents the width of the rectangle. It&rsquo;s given that a rectangle has a length of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"56\"><mn>56</mn></math> inches and a width of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"28\"><mn>28</mn></math> inches. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"56\"><mn>56</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"28\"><mn>28</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi></math> in the formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals script l w\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mi>w</mi></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals left parenthesis 56 right parenthesis left parenthesis 28 right parenthesis\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals 1,568\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1,568</mn></math>. Therefore, the area, in square inches, of the rectangle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"1,568\"><mn>1,568</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This is the width, in inches, not the area, in square inches, of the rectangle.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1776362727992,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"9d2e7037","skill_cd":"S.A.","score_band_range_cd":2,"skill_desc":