\"><mn>56</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"28\"><mn>28</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi></math> in the formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals script l w\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mi>w</mi></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals left parenthesis 56 right parenthesis left parenthesis 28 right parenthesis\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>28</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper A equals 1,568\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1,568</mn></math>. Therefore, the area, in square inches, of the rectangle is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"1,568\"><mn>1,568</mn></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This is the width, in inches, not the area, in square inches, of the rectangle.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","externalid":"5a173e5b-ac90-4f05-806e-fe38d80fcfd9","correct_answer":["D"]},"createDate":1776362727992,"updateDate":1776362727992}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1776362727992, 1776362727992),
    ($SATQ$9e44284b$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$01735-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.D.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Circles$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">In the&nbsp;<span class="italic"><span class="italic ">xy</span></span>-plane, the graph of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9e44284b/img_002_2dc913be.png" alt="2 x squared, minus 6 x, plus 2 y squared, plus 2 y, equals 45"></span> is a circle. What is the radius of the circle?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p>5</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p>6.5</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9e44284b/img_000_66b544dc.png\" alt=\"square root of 40\"></span>&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9e44284b/img_001_67df124c.png\" alt=\"square root of 50\"></span>&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is correct. One way to find the radius of the circle is to rewrite the given equation in standard form, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9e44284b/img_003_b7cf5f79.png" alt="open parenthesis, x minus h, close parenthesis, squared, plus, open parenthesis, y minus k, close parenthesis, squared, equals r squared"></span>, where <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9e44284b/img_004_bc099316.png" alt="the ordered pair h comma k"></span> is the center of the circle and the radius of the circle is <span class="italic">r</span>. To do this, divide the original equation, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9e44284b/img_005_2dc913be.png" alt="2 x squared, minus 6 x, plus 2 y squared, plus 2 y, equals 45"></span>, by 2 to make the leading coefficients of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9e44284b/img_006_572bc813.png" alt="x squared"></span> and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9e44284b/img_007_03ef89a8.png" alt="y squared"></span> each equal to 1:&nbsp;<span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9e44284b/img_008_d32cba37.png" alt="as follows: x squared, minus 3 x, plus y squared, plus y, equals 22 point 5"></span>. Then complete the square to put the equation in standard form. To do so, first rewrite <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9e44284b/img_009_d32cba37.png" alt="x squared, minus 3 x, plus y squared, plus y, equals 22 point 5"></span> as <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9e44284b/img_010_6858f050.png" alt="open parenthesis, x squared, minus 3 x, plus 2 point 2 5, close parenthesis, minus 2 point 2 5, plus, open parenthesis, y squared, plus y, plus 0 point 2 5, close parenthesis, minus 0 point 2 5, equals 22 point 5"></span>. Second, add 2.25 and 0.25 to both sides of the equation: <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9e44284b/img_011_617a2cbe.png" alt="open parenthesis, x squared, minus 3 x, plus 2 point 2 5, close parenthesis, plus, open parenthesis, y squared, plus y, plus 0 point 2 5, close parenthesis, equals 25"></span>. Since <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9e44284b/img_012_04961a64.png" alt="x squared, minus 3 x, plus 2 point 2 5, equals, open parenthesis, x minus 1 point 5, close parenthesis, squared"></span>, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9e44284b/img_013_17c0f0a8.png" alt="y squared, plus y, plus 0 point 2 5, equals, open parenthesis, y plus 0 point 5, close parenthesis, squared"></span>, and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9e44284b/img_014_23786863.png" alt="25 equals 5 squared"></span>, it follows that <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9e44284b/img_015_5f617b6d.png" alt="open parenthesis, x minus 1 point 5, close parenthesis, squared, plus, open parenthesis, y plus 0 point 5, close parenthesis, squared, equals 5 squared"></span>. Therefore, the radius of the circle is 5.<p>Choices B, C, and D are incorrect and may be the result of errors in manipulating the equation or of a misconception about the standard form of the equation of a circle in the <span class="italic">xy</span>-plane.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
$SATQ$, false, 16, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$Multiple Choice$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"9e44284b","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"01735-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.D.","skill_desc":"Circles","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">In the&nbsp;<span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"italic \">xy</span></span>-plane, the graph of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9e44284b/img_002_2dc913be.png\" alt=\"2 x squared, minus 6 x, plus 2 y squared, plus 2 y, equals 45\"></span> is a circle. What is the radius of the circle?</p>\n","answerOptions":[{"id":"a","content":"<p>5</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p>6.5</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9e44284b/img_000_66b544dc.png\" alt=\"square root of 40\"></span>&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9e44284b/img_001_67df124c.png\" alt=\"square root of 50\"></span>&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;</p>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is correct. One way to find the radius of the circle is to rewrite the given equation in standard form, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/9e44284b/img_003_b7cf5f79.png\" alt=\"open parenthes