,0,0,0,.494-1.182.277.277,0,0,1,.271-.213.591.591,0,0,1,.35.077q-.467,2.326-.524,2.714a.338.338,0,0,1-.388.31h-6.357c-.051,0-.1-.075-.145-.223a1.314,1.314,0,0,1-.068-.359,28.786,28.786,0,0,0,3.625-4.428,7.539,7.539,0,0,0,1.511-3.886,2.309,2.309,0,0,0-.523-1.618,1.78,1.78,0,0,0-1.376-.572,2.918,2.918,0,0,0-2.578,1.609.357.357,0,0,1-.242-.126c-.084-.084-.126-.145-.126-.184a2.306,2.306,0,0,1,.32-.63,6.964,6.964,0,0,1,.7-.872,3.65,3.65,0,0,1,1.162-.814A3.6,3.6,0,0,1,154.512,62.609Z\" fill=\"#231f20\"></path></g></svg><div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for diagram of 2 intersecting lines\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul>\n<li>At the intersection of the 2 lines, the angles are labeled clockwise from left as follows:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>Left: 1</li>\n<li>Top: unlabeled</li>\n<li>Right: 2</li>\n<li>Bottom: unlabeled</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>A note indicates the figure is not drawn to scale.</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the figure, two lines intersect at a point. Angle <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math> and angle <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> are vertical angles. The measure of angle <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"72 degree\"><mn>72</mn>\n<mo>&#176;</mo></math>. What is the measure of angle <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"5ad18cf1-fdb5-4431-a5d2-cd1b9be8c292","content":"<p><math alttext=\"72 degree\"><mn>72</mn>\n<mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"c1e16bd3-5e37-47f1-b043-efae979c0090","content":"<p><math alttext=\"108 degree\"><mn>108</mn>\n<mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"dbb05c22-bbe0-4137-9819-8fc8f06214cb","content":"<p><math alttext=\"144 degree\"><mn>144</mn>\n<mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"9d4d01af-e2d7-4fd4-a005-62be25e6d3b5","content":"<p><math alttext=\"288 degree\"><mn>288</mn>\n<mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"}],"keys":["5ad18cf1-fdb5-4431-a5d2-cd1b9be8c292"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. It&rsquo;s given that angle <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math> and angle <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> are vertical angles, and the measure of angle <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"72 degree\"><mn>72</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. Vertical angles have equal measures. Therefore, the measure of angle <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"72 degree\"><mn>72</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This is the measure of an angle that is supplementary, not congruent, to angle <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. This is the sum of the measures of angle <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math> and angle <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1730147357408,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"a456f28c","skill_cd":"S.B.","score_band_range_cd":1,"skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","createDate":1730147357408,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"","external_id":"a79dbc7d-8d01-40c4-8900-15940eeff7d7","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"8d26f92c-fb0e-403c-9fd0-06b0ac182c54","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"answerOptions":[{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"72 degree\"><mn>72</mn>\n<mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>","id":"5ad18cf1-fdb5-4431-a5d2-cd1b9be8c292"},{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"108 degree\"><mn>108</mn>\n<mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>","id":"c1e16bd3-5e37-47f1-b043-efae979c0090"},{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"144 degree\"><mn>144</mn>\n<mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>","id":"dbb05c22-bbe0-4137-9819-8fc8f06214cb"},{"content":"<p><math alttext=\"288 degree\"><mn>288</mn>\n<mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>","id":"9d4d01af-e2d7-4fd4-a005-62be25e6d3b5"}],"externalid":"a79dbc7d-8d01-40c4-8900-15940eeff7d7","keys":["5ad18cf1-fdb5-4431-a5d2-cd1b9be8c292"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. It&rsquo;s given that angle <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math> and angle <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> are vertical angles, and the measure of angle <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"72 degree\"><mn>72</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. Vertical angles have equal measures. Therefore, the measure of angle <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"72 degree\"><mn>72</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This is the measure of an angle that is supplementary, not congruent, to angle <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. This is the sum of the measures of angle <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math> and angle <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"247.442\" height=\"181.721\" viewBox=\"0 0 247.442 181.721\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A diagram of 2 intersecting lines. Refer to long description.\"><g id=\"b03ae3f7-ba50-4ccf-9b81-f730f6761bb1\" data-name=\"Layer 1\"><line x1=\"242.494\" y1=\"0.945\" x2=\"5.685\" y2=\"137.667\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#231f20\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-width=\"1.89\"></line><line x1=\"5.685\" y1=\"0.945\" x2=\"242.494\" y2=\"137.667\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#231f20\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-width=\"1.89\"></line><path d=\"M10.291,167.166a7.565,7.565,0,0,0-.136-1.7c-.039-.1-.261-.2-.669-.3a4.335,4.335,0,0,0-.862-.145c-.052,0-.078-.074-.078-.223a.427.427,0,0,1,.078-.3q.252.02,1.008.067t1.